        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-14T09:17:54+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-14T09:17:54+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-13T23:47:54Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-13T23:47:54Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure ridge builds across much of SA, as a cold front slips across southern coasts late today into early Tuesday. A high pressure system will then move across waters to the south throughout the week to be centred over Victoria by Thursday. A low pressure trough in the interior of WA may extend into far western parts at times before weakening by late Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
